<!DOCTYPE node PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD D-BUS Object Introspection 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/introspect.dtd">
<!--
  The plugin host on the session bus (plans/PLAN-plugins.md). amethystora-plugin-host owns the name org.amethystora.Plugins
  while at least one plugin is on; the shell's `plugins` module (a later phase), Control and Security are its clients. This file
  is the contract between them: change it with the plan.

  Conventions
   - Callers are known by the file they run (/proc/PID/exe of the connection): GNOME Shell, Control and Security. Any other
     program of the account is refused (org.amethystora.Plugins.Error.NotAvailable), and a signal goes only to a caller that
     asked something.
   - Everything a plugin printed has been read, refused or cleaned by the host (output.rs) before it is here: text without markup,
     icons as theme names, at most twenty elements in a card. Clients still clamp it again, and draw it as text.
   - A plugin's id is its reverse-domain name. The host does the work; a client keeps nothing.
-->
<node>
  <interface name="org.amethystora.Plugins">
    <!-- A JSON array, one object for each plugin that is on: {"id", "name", "version", "output", "error", "paused", "reason",
         "waiting", "places", "author", "draft", "shipped", "granted", "actions", "sample"}. "output" is what its last run printed, as the host
         passed it, or null; "error" says why the last run failed, or is empty; "places" is where it is drawn (the manifest's "contributes",
         each surface with its options); "draft" is an agent's draft, which runs with nothing granted and shows "sample" when its run finds
         nothing to reach; "waiting" is "vault" while its secret settings are in a closed Vault -->
    <method name="List">
      <arg type="s" name="plugins" direction="out"/>
    </method>
    <!-- Runs one of the plugin's own actions, which its manifest names. The answer comes as Updated; this returns at once -->
    <method name="Action">
      <arg type="s" name="id" direction="in"/>
      <arg type="s" name="action" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <!-- Stops a plugin running until Resume. Nothing is granted or taken away by it -->
    <method name="Pause">
      <arg type="s" name="id" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <method name="Resume">
      <arg type="s" name="id" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <!-- A plugin printed something new (the same object List gives), or failed -->
    <signal name="Updated">
      <arg type="s" name="id"/>
      <arg type="s" name="plugin"/>
    </signal>
    <!-- A plugin paused itself, once, and why: "crash" (five runs in a row failed), "slow" (three hit the 30 seconds), "memory" (two went
         over their memory), "updates" (more than 30 results in a minute). A person's own Pause says "person" in List and sends nothing -->
    <signal name="Paused">
      <arg type="s" name="id"/>
      <arg type="s" name="reason"/>
    </signal>
    <!-- A plugin asked, after a click on its own element and with the permission, for the shell to do what only it can: kind "open" (a web
         address, which the shell shows before it opens) or "clipboard" (a text, written once; there is no clipboard read) -->
    <signal name="Asked">
      <arg type="s" name="id"/>
      <arg type="s" name="kind"/>
      <arg type="s" name="text"/>
    </signal>
    <!-- Sending to a host passed its limit and it is blocked until a person decides (Keep blocked, or Allow, which asks for an
         administrator's approval) -->
    <signal name="OverLimit">
      <arg type="s" name="id"/>
      <arg type="s" name="host"/>
    </signal>
  </interface>
</node>
